{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>On the border of the Emorites.</b> The boundary at the end of their territory — and so גְּבוּל מוֹאָב is the same: a term of edge and end." "<b>The crossing of the Arnon.</b> They circled the land of Moab along its entire south and east side until they came to the other bank of the Arnon, within the land of the Emorites on the north side of the land of Moab." "<b>Which extends from the border of the Emorites.</b> A strip of land projects from the border of the Emorites — it belongs to the Emorites — and enters the territory of Moab as far as the Arnon, which is the border of Moab. There Israel encamped, and they did not enter the territory of Moab, <b>for the Arnon is the border of Moab</b> — and Moab did not give them permission to pass through their land. And even though Moses did not spell this out, Jephthah did, as Jephthah said (Judges 11): ״וְגַם אֶל מֶלֶךְ מוֹאָב שָׁלַח וְלֹא אָבָה״ — and Moses alluded to it (Deuteronomy 2): ״כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ לִי בְּנֵי עֵשָׂו הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּשֵׂעִיר וְהַמּוֹאָבִים הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּעָר״ — just as these did not let them pass through their land but forced them to go around, so too did Moab."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:58.547864631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}